 "pattern": "Reverse k nodes, recurse on the rest",
 "statement": "Reverse the nodes of a linked list `k` at a time and return the new head. If fewer than `k` nodes remain at the end, leave them in their original order. Only the links may change, not the values.",
 "example": {
  "input": "head = [1,2,3,4,5], k = 2",
  "output": "[2,1,4,3,5]",
  "why": "1,2 becomes 2,1 and 3,4 becomes 4,3. The single node 5 is fewer than k, so it stays."
 },
